WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.831
npm account security protects the
authority to publish, update, deprecate,

2
00:00:07.911 --> 00:00:09.828
or manage packages.

3
00:00:09.908 --> 00:00:16.449
A compromised maintainer account can
affect many downstream users,

4
00:00:16.529 --> 00:00:23.409
and a compromised organization account can
disrupt internal delivery.

5
00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:30.820
Teams should enforce strong
authentication, review membership regularly,

6
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:39.246
remove stale maintainers, and separate
human publishing access from automation where

7
00:00:39.326 --> 00:00:40.341
possible.

8
00:00:40.421 --> 00:00:47.413
Publishing rights should be treated like
production deployment rights.

9
00:00:47.493 --> 00:00:51.892
Tokens should be scoped, protected,
rotated,

10
00:00:51.972 --> 00:00:59.190
and stored in a secret manager rather than
copied into scripts, local files,

11
00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.413
or broad CI variables.

12
00:01:01.493 --> 00:01:08.485
Automation tokens should have the minimum
permission needed for the job.

13
00:01:08.565 --> 00:01:16.121
A token used only to install private
packages should not also publish releases.

14
00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:23.758
A token used for one project should not
unlock every package in an organization.

15
00:01:23.838 --> 00:01:31.845
Smaller blast radius makes credential
exposure less damaging and easier to respond

16
00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:32.264
to.

17
00:01:32.344 --> 00:01:40.464
Trusted publishing and provenance features
can improve confidence by tying package

18
00:01:40.544 --> 00:01:46.408
publication to a known build workflow and
source repository.

19
00:01:46.488 --> 00:01:50.887
They do not make a package automatically
safe,

20
00:01:50.967 --> 00:01:55.027
but they help answer important questions:

21
00:01:55.107 --> 00:02:03.002
what workflow produced this artifact,
under what identity, and from which source.

22
00:02:03.082 --> 00:02:09.623
Combined with code review, release
approvals, branch protections,

23
00:02:09.703 --> 00:02:12.861
and package ownership controls,

24
00:02:12.941 --> 00:02:18.580
publishing evidence makes npm delivery
more accountable.
